1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,460
(All child actor scenes were filmed with a guardian present...)

2
00:00:01,530 --> 00:00:03,000
(with professional staff and in accordance with safety guidelines.)

3
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:38,970
Won Ho.

4
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:42,310
Wait a minute.

5
00:00:58,490 --> 00:00:59,490
Let's...

6
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:02,960
Let's get divorced.

7
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:31,120
(Episode 1)

8
00:01:56,710 --> 00:02:00,420
Hello, my followers. Good morning.

9
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:04,520
Looks like more people are joining.

10
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:06,590
Shall we begin? Yes.

11
00:02:07,290 --> 00:02:09,090
Hello, my followers.

12
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:13,200
Do you know what today is?

13
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,370
Today is the special day we at J&White...

14
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:19,540
are so excited to present our free dress-fitting event.

15
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:24,940
For all you brides-to-be out there,

16
00:02:25,010 --> 00:02:26,580
when you're out dress shopping,

17
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:28,780
the fees for trying on each dress...

18
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:31,210
can be a real burden, can't they?

19
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,780
If you visit us at J&White today,

20
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:36,420
you can try on as many dresses as you like,

21
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:38,290
not for half off, but for free.

22
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:39,490
(I want to see your husband.)

23
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,060
My husband?

24
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,760
(An opportunity like this doesn't come often.)

25
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:43,960
It sure doesn't.

26
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:46,630
So be sure to come and see my husband in person.

27
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:50,530
But this is a little secret just between us.

28
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,600
My husband's heart is even more handsome than his face.

29
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:56,910
Even today, just for me,

30
00:02:57,170 --> 00:03:00,240
he made me fresh juice before he went to work.

31
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:01,540
(You're so pretty. Will Designer Ji be there?)

32
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:02,710
(Will we get to see him in person?)

33
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:05,820
Anyway, my dear followers,

34
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:09,720
I put so much effort into preparing today's event,

35
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:12,860
so don't miss this opportunity. Please visit our store today.

36
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:17,590
It starts at 11:00 a.m. Okay, see you all later. Bye.

37
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:19,360
(See you at the store. I've been waiting for this day.)

38
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:20,500
(Livestream ended)

39
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:41,180
The forecast for today is mostly clear skies nationwide,

40
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:43,190
with some occasional clouds.

41
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:46,860
Thick fog has formed in the inland regions this morning,

42
00:03:46,990 --> 00:03:50,630
so please be cautious during your morning commute.

43
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:52,730
Strong winds are expected in mountains...

44
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,360
and along the east coast in Gangwon Province.

45
00:04:40,010 --> 00:04:41,040
Good morning.

46
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,550
Not for me.

47
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:45,680
I am in a terrible mood right now.

48
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,620
Is something wrong?

49
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:50,050
Do you really need to ask?

50
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:52,690
Take a good, hard look at yourself.

51
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:56,260
Manager Song, did I do something wrong?

52
00:04:56,390 --> 00:04:59,160
You went drinking again last night, didn't you?

53
00:04:59,530 --> 00:05:01,430
Yes, I did.

54
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:04,630
Don't you have any self-control?

55
00:05:04,870 --> 00:05:07,570
I try, but it's not that easy...

56
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:11,570
Then why do you keep breaking your promise, you idiot?

57
00:05:16,810 --> 00:05:20,120
You're not an ex-husband, you're my nemesis.

58
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,690
Vice President Kang.

59
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:30,860
Good morning.

60
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:33,330
- Yes. - Good morning.

61
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,440
Company sales have been dropping lately,

62
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,500
so let's make today's event a success...

63
00:05:41,870 --> 00:05:43,640
and really turn things around.

64
00:05:45,070 --> 00:05:46,080
- Yes. - Yes.

65
00:05:46,410 --> 00:05:47,980
You two, prepare the pamphlets...

66
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:50,010
and dress lists so you can immediately...

67
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:52,050
answer any questions customers have when they arrive.

68
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:54,980
We'll get a lot of customers this time, right?

69
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:58,490
Of course. CEO Baek worked so hard on this event.

70
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:01,590
This event will be a success, and company sales will soar.

71
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:02,960
Let's do this.

72
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:06,660
Oh, and please finish the showroom display this morning.

73
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:09,300
I already finished that.

74
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,770
I just checked, and there was nothing there.

75
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:14,240
What? That can't be right.

76
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:18,980
Hey. What do you think you're doing?

77
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:20,840
Where are the dresses that were here?

78
00:06:21,110 --> 00:06:25,010
CEO Ji called and told me to replace them with these.

79
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:28,220
CEO Ji?

80
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:31,050
It's fine.

81
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,960
Just do what CEO Ji wants.

82
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,630
- Okay. - Really?

83
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,900
But you worked on that display day and night.

84
00:06:42,130 --> 00:06:46,070
Well, we have to respect the opinion...

85
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:47,800
of a J&White designer.

86
00:06:49,410 --> 00:06:50,710
Excuse me? Is anyone here?

87
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,440
Yes. Welcome.

88
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:56,180
- I'm here for a dress quote. - Of course.

89
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:57,580
No, I'll take care of it.

90
00:06:58,350 --> 00:06:59,550
I can help you.

91
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,820
Yes, please fill this out.

92
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,520
CEO Baek is really...

93
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:08,120
She's such a class act.

94
00:07:11,790 --> 00:07:12,900
I'm Baek Mi Young.

95
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:16,170
The CEO of the all-in-one wedding company, J&White.

96
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:21,600
For my company, there's nothing I won't do or can't accomplish.

97
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:24,540
I think any of these would look good on you.

98
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:25,540
Then please choose one...

99
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:26,640
Yes, ma'am.

100
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,810
Yes, the preliminary fitting is done.

101
00:07:28,910 --> 00:07:31,850
Yes, you just need to come in for one more fitting.

102
00:07:32,010 --> 00:07:33,720
You're not available?

103
00:07:34,350 --> 00:07:37,890
In that case, I can bring the dress to you.

104
00:07:37,890 --> 00:07:38,890
Yes, of course.

105
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,790
If a path is blocked, I forge a new one.

106
00:07:43,190 --> 00:07:46,800
If there's something I don't know, I learn it to get the job done.

107
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:52,740
But even I had a mountain I couldn't easily climb.

108
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,440
The famous designer, Ji Won Ho.

109
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:00,880
My husband.

110
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:05,350
(Special Event: Free Fitting Event for Brides- And Grooms-To-Be)

111
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:08,020
(Free Fitting for Brides-To-Be)

112
00:08:14,290 --> 00:08:16,290
This one needs to have the same beads.

113
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,300
I can't stand the sight of him.

114
00:08:32,510 --> 00:08:34,140
I can't believe people throw trash on the floor...

115
00:08:34,210 --> 00:08:38,180
when the can is right there. I'm so sick of it. Seriously.

116
00:08:42,990 --> 00:08:45,620
- What do you think you're doing? - You'll clean it up anyway.

117
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,590
(Jihwaja Motel)

118
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:49,660
Excuse me.

119
00:08:49,930 --> 00:08:52,660
Come on, you can't just throw that at someone.

120
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:54,460
So what?

121
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,500
Let go.

122
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:00,470
Disgusting.

123
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:02,470
You're just a motel cleaner.

124
00:09:08,710 --> 00:09:10,150
(Jihwaja Motel)

125
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:11,280
That son of a...

126
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:40,210
Hey, you punk.

127
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,480
What?

128
00:10:00,130 --> 00:10:01,130
(Jihwaja Motel)

129
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:03,770
I told you to control that temper.

130
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:07,170
What were you thinking, throwing something at a guest?

131
00:10:07,570 --> 00:10:09,570
You're lucky I was able to calm him down with an apology.

132
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,610
Mom, you're going to get arrested doing that.

133
00:10:11,670 --> 00:10:13,510
My son was being humiliated.

134
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,910
What parent would just stand by and watch that?

135
00:10:16,210 --> 00:10:17,680
Still, you can't just do that to a guest.

136
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:20,650
Guest or not, family always comes first.

137
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:22,850
Right, Ha Neul?

138
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,520
Yes, Grandma is the best.

139
00:10:24,690 --> 00:10:27,320
Oh, you're such a sweet little thing.

140
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:30,660
Anyway,

141
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:33,900
you know what this weekend is, right?

142
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:36,200
It's the weekend, so it's when the soap opera is on.

143
00:10:36,370 --> 00:10:39,040
Hey, you punk. You don't even know your own mother's birthday?

144
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:42,140
Everything about you is bad,

145
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:44,170
but your memory is the worst. Got it?

146
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:49,250
Speaking of which, you know my friend Gi Sun, right?

147
00:10:51,210 --> 00:10:52,720
Her daughter-in-law, you know,

148
00:10:52,950 --> 00:10:55,050
apparently prepared a birthday feast for her...

149
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:56,250
that was fit for a king.

150
00:10:56,590 --> 00:10:59,260
Some women have all the luck.

151
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:00,720
What daughter-in-law cooks a birthday meal...

152
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:01,790
for her mother-in-law these days?

153
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:03,260
I'm serious.

154
00:11:03,790 --> 00:11:06,400
Mom, don't even think about it.

155
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:08,630
Maybe some spending money or a trip, but a birthday meal?

156
00:11:09,070 --> 00:11:10,930
My mom sure has big dreams.

157
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:14,170
What? Big dreams? You brat!

158
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:16,470
- Ha Neul, it's time for preschool. - Okay.

159
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:17,540
Say goodbye to Grandma.

160
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:20,540
- Goodbye. - Bye, Ha Neul.

161
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:27,380
(Happy Birthday)

162
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:29,390
Right.

163
00:11:30,090 --> 00:11:33,460
I'm going to have my daughter-in-law make me a birthday meal.

164
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:54,940
It hurts to look.

165
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:57,850
How can there not even be...

166
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,920
one person here?

167
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:05,250
It's the recession, I suppose.

168
00:12:07,290 --> 00:12:09,460
Are we going to go out of business at this rate?

169
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:10,990
Out of business?

170
00:12:11,790 --> 00:12:12,800
Director Song.

171
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,160
You take that back right now.

172
00:12:14,430 --> 00:12:16,730
- Take it back. - I take it back.

173
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:20,500
I guess...

174
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,640
the event wasn't promoted as well as we'd hoped.

175
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:25,910
It wasn't just "not promoted", it was completely wrong.

176
00:12:27,310 --> 00:12:28,710
The focus was all wrong.

177
00:12:29,450 --> 00:12:30,980
Instead of doing some pointless free event,

178
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:33,520
we should've been promoting the kinds of dresses we actually sell.

179
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,650
Show that J&White is different from other shops.

180
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:39,420
That we have something special.

181
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:42,290
That's why I told you from the start this was a bad idea.

182
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:48,030
I was right, wasn't I?

183
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:56,010
(Free Fitting for Brides-To-Be)

184
00:12:57,910 --> 00:12:59,010
Welcome.

185
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:00,980
Hello.

186
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,580
Are you here for our event?

187
00:13:03,910 --> 00:13:04,980
Actually, no.

188
00:13:05,210 --> 00:13:07,550
I'm here to see the CEOs.

189
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,250
The CEOs?

190
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,060
(Dream Project: Wedding Edition)

191
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,290
(Kim Hye Won, Writer, CSB)

192
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:17,860
You want to cast us in a variety show?

193
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:21,660
Yes. Have you ever heard of a show called "Dream Project"?

194
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:27,400
Oh, I know that show.

195
00:13:27,770 --> 00:13:31,010
It's the one with all the famous experts...

196
00:13:31,070 --> 00:13:32,940
who grant wishes for regular people.

197
00:13:33,510 --> 00:13:35,080
- That one? - Yes.

198
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:38,010
- Didn't they build a house once? - Oh, yes.

199
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:39,520
Yes, that's the one.

200
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:42,690
So this time around, we're planning a wedding theme.

201
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:45,520
For people who couldn't have a wedding due to their circumstances,

202
00:13:45,790 --> 00:13:47,490
we'll be making them their wedding dresses.

203
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:50,760
What do you think?

204
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,760
It sounds like a great project.

205
00:13:52,830 --> 00:13:53,830
Yes.

206
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:55,560
And now that I'm seeing you in person.

207
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:56,700
CEO Ji,

208
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:59,240
you're much more handsome than in your photos.

209
00:13:59,770 --> 00:14:04,010
Why haven't you ever been on television before?

210
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:09,510
Right? Our CEO Ji is even more handsome in person.

211
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:13,480
Well,

212
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:18,050
CEO Ji is a little introverted.

213
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:22,860
- Could CEO Baek go on by herself... - No.

214
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:25,390
I absolutely need both of you to be on the show.

215
00:14:27,030 --> 00:14:29,100
Both of us?

216
00:14:29,330 --> 00:14:31,030
Yes. The program's content...

217
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:33,040
is about couples' stories, so we're looking...

218
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,870
for a married couple to be on the show.

219
00:14:35,570 --> 00:14:36,570
I see.

220
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:38,140
Yes, and in that regard,

221
00:14:38,610 --> 00:14:40,480
you two are the perfect fit.

222
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:43,950
Besides, I hear you're a famously devoted couple.

223
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:51,990
That's right.

224
00:14:52,050 --> 00:14:55,760
Our two CEOs are incredibly close.

225
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:58,060
You've definitely come to the right place.

226
00:14:58,830 --> 00:15:02,870
Even lovebirds have nothing on them.

227
00:15:06,770 --> 00:15:09,510
So, will you give it some thought?

228
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:17,510
(Free Fitting for Brides-To-Be)

229
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,720
- Please watch your step. - Okay, thank you.

230
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:21,120
- Goodbye. - Goodbye.

231
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,480
- Take care. - You too.

232
00:15:24,490 --> 00:15:25,490
Hurry.

233
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,990
I'm not doing it.

234
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,620
Sir.

235
00:15:29,190 --> 00:15:30,790
Don't just say you won't do it.

236
00:15:31,090 --> 00:15:32,700
Try to be more positive about it.

237
00:15:32,830 --> 00:15:34,630
Positive or not, I can't do things like that.

238
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:37,170
- I won't. - Why can't you do it?

239
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,930
Not that I expected you to,

240
00:15:39,230 --> 00:15:41,400
but let's at least hear why. Why won't you do it?

241
00:15:43,310 --> 00:15:44,440
Because it's like being a clown.

242
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:45,610
A clown?

243
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:47,740
Pretending you agree when you don't, pretending you like things you hate,

244
00:15:47,810 --> 00:15:49,010
sucking up to people,

245
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,480
and acting like a phony.

246
00:15:50,650 --> 00:15:51,950
What's that if not a clown?

247
00:15:52,610 --> 00:15:54,050
I don't want to stoop to that level.

248
00:15:57,250 --> 00:15:58,790
That is so you.

249
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:00,620
You don't care what happens to the company...

250
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,290
or if our employees starve.

251
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,460
Even if your life depended on it, you...

252
00:16:03,530 --> 00:16:04,630
Even if my life depended on it, what?

253
00:16:04,690 --> 00:16:06,700
You'd still refuse to listen to anything I say.

254
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:07,900
Just to be contrary.

255
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:09,800
What?

256
00:16:10,730 --> 00:16:12,740
Let's just go inside, Mi Young.

257
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,270
Stop acting so high and mighty.

258
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:15,570
You think you own this company?

259
00:16:16,710 --> 00:16:17,740
Oh, no.

260
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:19,840
Here we go.

261
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:25,850
Hey. You think you're successful because you're so special?

262
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:30,050
No, designers like you are a dime a dozen in this country.

263
00:16:30,350 --> 00:16:34,120
The Ji Won Ho brand name was built on me playing the clown.

264
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:35,820
Do you get it? Do you have any idea?

265
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:38,530
- Mi Young, stop. - And another thing,

266
00:16:38,590 --> 00:16:40,260
even a clown wouldn't wear those pants.

267
00:16:40,330 --> 00:16:43,600
- Your knees have holes, you idiot. - Stop it.

268
00:16:44,030 --> 00:16:46,840
- You really... - Just stop.

269
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:48,870
- Hey. - Seriously.

270
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:56,550
You scared me.

271
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:58,810
What is all this?

272
00:16:59,010 --> 00:17:00,320
J&White's last quarter's...

273
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:02,220
financial statements and sales summary.

274
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:05,250
Ji Won Ho needs to see this. That company's sales are falling.

275
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:07,790
Maybe he'll come to his senses if he sees it with his own eyes.

276
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:09,590
But...

277
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:11,190
do you think that will work?

278
00:17:12,530 --> 00:17:15,460
If you want to persuade him,

279
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:20,270
don't you think you need to humour him a little?

280
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:22,270
How much more? What else is there?

281
00:17:22,940 --> 00:17:24,070
I've always put up with...

282
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:25,770
Ji Won Ho and catered to his every whim.

283
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:28,840
This is the last straw. I can't take it anymore.

284
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:35,720
Yes.

285
00:17:35,850 --> 00:17:37,850
We've secured evidence of assault by the defendant,

286
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,820
so we can take away his custody and parental rights.

287
00:17:39,890 --> 00:17:40,990
Don't worry.

288
00:17:41,490 --> 00:17:44,160
I'll give you the details in person when we meet tomorrow.

289
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,800
We can meet at the café by your house like last time, right?

290
00:17:51,530 --> 00:17:52,600
It's no trouble at all.

291
00:17:54,470 --> 00:17:56,940
I'm much more comfortable going there myself.

292
00:17:57,710 --> 00:17:58,710
And when it comes to evidence,

293
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:01,310
I prefer to collect it myself.

294
00:18:05,310 --> 00:18:06,420
I'll see you tomorrow.

295
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:17,830
Ms. Baek Mi Young.

296
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:23,000
Chi Hyun.

297
00:18:23,530 --> 00:18:26,200
Hello. Fancy seeing you here.

298
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:28,540
I know, right? You remember her, don't you?

299
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,740
Our manager.

300
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:31,610
Hello. I was the one...

301
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:33,940
who helped you with your dress fitting.

302
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:36,810
Of course, I remember. It was my dress of a lifetime.

303
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,680
If I get the chance,

304
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:40,750
I'll come back to renew it.

305
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:43,390
- What? - Renew?

306
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:45,420
I got divorced recently.

307
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,090
I see.

308
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,690
Oh my, I had no idea.

309
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:51,860
Well, things like that happen.

310
00:18:52,330 --> 00:18:53,800
If you ever need me, give me a call.

311
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,430
(Jeon Chi Hyun, Divorce Lawyer, Specialist in Affairs)

312
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:58,070
I knew you were a lawyer, but...

313
00:18:58,270 --> 00:19:01,070
"Affairs"?

314
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:03,340
Hey, what's with you? Read the room.

315
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:07,040
Of course, it's best if nothing happens,

316
00:19:07,510 --> 00:19:08,940
but you never know with life.

317
00:19:10,050 --> 00:19:11,280
Well, I should get going.

318
00:19:17,750 --> 00:19:21,220
A newly divorced divorce lawyer.

319
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:25,130
She seems really tough, don't you think, Mi Young?

320
00:19:25,190 --> 00:19:27,130
Still, hearing a former client got divorced,

321
00:19:27,330 --> 00:19:28,730
it just feels strange.

322
00:19:29,830 --> 00:19:31,400
I'm sure she had her reasons.

323
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:34,000
Hey, sit down.

324
00:19:34,370 --> 00:19:38,110
- All right, let's drink up. - Okay, sure.

325
00:19:38,210 --> 00:19:40,710
- Cheers. - Darn Ji Won Ho.

326
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:44,110
You went too far this time.

327
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,150
Mi Young is working so hard...

328
00:19:46,250 --> 00:19:47,420
to save the company.

329
00:19:47,780 --> 00:19:49,220
Hey, I'm trying too.

330
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:51,220
Do you have to make a big show of it to prove you're trying?

331
00:19:52,620 --> 00:19:53,720
You know, Kyung Tae,

332
00:19:53,790 --> 00:19:56,020
you tend to subtly take Baek Mi Young's side.

333
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:59,030
- Whose side are you on? - What? That's so childish.

334
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:03,070
Anyway, it's not like Mi Young was completely wrong.

335
00:20:03,130 --> 00:20:05,430
First of all, her tone is just insulting.

336
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:07,100
It's not like I'm her subordinate or something.

337
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:08,700
But...

338
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:10,510
are you really not going to do that variety show?

339
00:20:10,570 --> 00:20:11,570
I'm not doing it.

340
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:13,040
I'll never do it, not in a million years.

341
00:20:17,010 --> 00:20:19,650
I'm not asking her to walk on eggshells around me.

342
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:21,320
At the very least, there should be a minimum of...

343
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:23,450
respect between a husband and wife.

344
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:26,620
She treats me with less respect than a stray dog.

345
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:28,760
You two have been sleeping...

346
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:30,190
in separate rooms for a while, right?

347
00:20:32,890 --> 00:20:34,060
Yes, for about three years now.

348
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,730
Since you're sleeping in separate rooms,

349
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:38,100
you don't have a chance to fix your relationship.

350
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:41,800
If you're going to keep living like this,

351
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:43,640
then wouldn't it...

352
00:20:44,870 --> 00:20:46,110
be better to get a divorce?

353
00:20:49,310 --> 00:20:52,510
I just mean, if that's the case, wouldn't it be better for you...

354
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:53,850
to find your own happiness separately?

355
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:55,650
Life's too short.

356
00:20:56,350 --> 00:20:57,390
Darn it.

357
00:21:00,790 --> 00:21:02,060
Darn it.

358
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:12,900
Lately, I've been feeling like...

359
00:21:14,070 --> 00:21:18,040
no matter how fast or how long I run,

360
00:21:18,970 --> 00:21:20,940
I'm still stuck in the same place.

361
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:24,480
Like you're on a treadmill?

362
00:21:25,250 --> 00:21:26,380
A treadmill?

363
00:21:27,650 --> 00:21:28,950
Yes, something like that.

364
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:33,690
I want to go further,

365
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:36,360
all the way to the finish line.

366
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:39,030
It's because...

367
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,560
you're too ambitious.

368
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:46,100
You're always trying to do things better,

369
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:49,400
and trying to make everything perfect.

370
00:21:51,170 --> 00:21:52,270
I guess so.

371
00:21:53,740 --> 00:21:56,380
Even if all my dreams came true right now,

372
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:01,080
I'm sure I'd just develop a new longing.

373
00:22:03,490 --> 00:22:04,520
But, A Ri.

374
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:07,660
I...

375
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:10,830
I really want to launch my own brand.

376
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,900
Not J&White,

377
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:16,400
but Baek Mi Young.

378
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:18,830
A brand with only my name on it.

379
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,300
My very own brand.

380
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:27,680
And I want to feel what it's like...

381
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:30,580
to have a clear path ahead of me,

382
00:22:31,980 --> 00:22:33,150
Then go for it.

383
00:23:12,150 --> 00:23:13,160
CEO Baek.

384
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:15,220
I'm the writer who visited you earlier.

385
00:23:15,790 --> 00:23:16,830
About casting CEO Ji,

386
00:23:16,890 --> 00:23:19,060
we really need a decision by the end of today.

387
00:23:19,590 --> 00:23:20,600
If he can't do it,

388
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:23,000
we'll have to hurry and find another designer.

389
00:23:26,570 --> 00:23:28,140
Won Ho, the writer needs your decision by today...

390
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:30,040
What's this about a birthday meal all of a sudden?

391
00:23:30,370 --> 00:23:32,610
I'll just send you double your allowance.

392
00:23:33,380 --> 00:23:35,010
I don't know. Then you can call Mi Young,

393
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,810
and talk to her yourself.

394
00:23:36,980 --> 00:23:38,210
I don't know. I'm hanging up.

395
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:40,350
She's acting like a child.

396
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:43,080
You startled me.

397
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:44,820
When did you get here?

398
00:23:44,890 --> 00:23:45,920
Just now.

399
00:23:47,220 --> 00:23:49,660
What was that call about?

400
00:23:49,990 --> 00:23:52,460
It was my mom. Her birthday is coming up.

401
00:23:53,090 --> 00:23:54,830
She's suddenly asking for a birthday meal.

402
00:23:55,260 --> 00:23:56,430
A birthday meal from her daughter-in-law...

403
00:23:56,500 --> 00:23:57,630
is her biggest wish or something.

404
00:23:58,130 --> 00:23:59,130
I see.

405
00:24:00,770 --> 00:24:02,270
Forget it. Don't worry about it.

406
00:24:02,340 --> 00:24:04,240
It's not the first time my mom has made a fuss.

407
00:24:06,740 --> 00:24:08,280
I really should just turn this off.

408
00:24:10,980 --> 00:24:13,850
If you want to persuade him,

409
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:19,250
don't you think you need to humour him a little?

410
00:24:21,390 --> 00:24:23,590
- I'll do it. - Okay.

411
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,430
What? Do what?

412
00:24:26,490 --> 00:24:28,460
Making the birthday meal for your mother.

413
00:24:28,660 --> 00:24:29,660
I'll do it.

414
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:30,770
What are you talking about?

415
00:24:30,830 --> 00:24:31,830
Why would you do that all of a sudden?

416
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,640
Forget it. That's weird. Don't do it.

417
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:35,370
No, what's weird about it?

418
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:37,870
A daughter-in-law making a meal for her mother-in-law's birthday.

419
00:24:40,210 --> 00:24:41,710
You're just doing this because of that, aren't you?

420
00:24:42,410 --> 00:24:45,580
- What? - This won't make me go on the show.

421
00:24:45,710 --> 00:24:46,720
That's not it.

422
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:48,480
I've always wanted...

423
00:24:48,550 --> 00:24:50,390
to make a birthday meal for her.

424
00:24:51,550 --> 00:24:54,160
I've been too neglectful of her until now.

425
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:57,630
As her daughter-in-law, it's the right thing to do.

426
00:25:06,670 --> 00:25:07,700
Good grief.

427
00:25:08,270 --> 00:25:09,500
Hello, Mother.

428
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,740
Hello, Seung Ho.

429
00:25:11,040 --> 00:25:12,170
Hi, Ha Neul.

430
00:25:12,340 --> 00:25:13,940
Aunt Mi Young.

431
00:25:14,210 --> 00:25:15,880
Oh, Mi Young, you really came?

432
00:25:16,380 --> 00:25:17,380
Yes, I did.

433
00:25:17,910 --> 00:25:19,750
Mom, what are you doing? Mi Young is saying hello.

434
00:25:20,580 --> 00:25:23,950
Mi Young, you're going to make me a birthday meal yourself?

435
00:25:24,550 --> 00:25:26,150
Yes. It's nothing special,

436
00:25:26,220 --> 00:25:27,820
but I brought some things to prepare.

437
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:30,460
Well then, let's see what you can do.

438
00:25:30,530 --> 00:25:32,330
I can help with that...

439
00:25:34,260 --> 00:25:36,260
Your back is acting up, what are you trying to do?

440
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:37,600
You need to rest.

441
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:41,170
- It's okay. I'll help. - Oh, Won Ho.

442
00:25:41,770 --> 00:25:43,640
Go to my room and alter one of my dresses for me.

443
00:25:43,770 --> 00:25:46,740
I've gained weight, and the hem's completely torn.

444
00:25:46,810 --> 00:25:49,580
Fix your dress? Out of the blue?

445
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:52,210
Please, just fix it. I have nothing to wear.

446
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:54,520
Come here. Fix my dress.

447
00:25:55,580 --> 00:25:57,390
I have nothing to wear.

448
00:25:58,720 --> 00:26:01,260
I'm sorry about that.

449
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:04,430
Ha Neul, let's go. Let's get something to drink.

450
00:26:09,430 --> 00:26:12,300
Okay, where should I start?

451
00:26:52,740 --> 00:26:54,280
You should throw things like this out.

452
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:56,880
This is nice.

453
00:26:56,950 --> 00:26:58,750
(Mystery)

454
00:27:01,150 --> 00:27:02,320
What's that smell?

455
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:05,620
Is Mi Young cooking?

456
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:10,060
Smells delicious.

457
00:27:56,140 --> 00:27:57,140
Hey.

458
00:27:58,070 --> 00:27:59,810
Did you just throw that?

459
00:28:03,010 --> 00:28:04,650
There are some things you just don't throw.

460
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:08,550
If you don't want to do this, just say so.

461
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:12,420
No, Mother. It was an accident...

462
00:28:15,690 --> 00:28:16,690
Listen.

463
00:28:17,460 --> 00:28:19,160
Have you given up on having a child?

464
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:20,760
Pardon?

465
00:28:20,860 --> 00:28:23,830
Why are you so skinny?

466
00:28:23,930 --> 00:28:26,430
You look even thinner than last time.

467
00:28:27,140 --> 00:28:28,570
Don't tell me you've given up...

468
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:30,570
just because you failed once, have you?

469
00:28:32,510 --> 00:28:35,140
You need some meat on your bones to get pregnant.

470
00:28:35,410 --> 00:28:37,250
Just because you're the same age as Won Ho,

471
00:28:37,310 --> 00:28:39,480
you can't think you're the same as him. Okay?

472
00:28:39,610 --> 00:28:42,750
A man can have children until the day he dies.

473
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:44,390
But a woman...

474
00:28:45,050 --> 00:28:47,320
I don't have to spell it out, do I?

475
00:28:50,990 --> 00:28:54,230
A child who looks like Won Ho would be so smart and beautiful.

476
00:29:24,260 --> 00:29:28,230
- Ha Neul, did you pick a book? - Yes. Please read me this one.

477
00:29:28,300 --> 00:29:30,430
Okay, bring it here.

478
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:33,640
(The Butterfly's Dream)

479
00:29:33,970 --> 00:29:35,840
Okay.

480
00:29:36,670 --> 00:29:38,210
But Auntie,

481
00:29:38,310 --> 00:29:40,280
are your clothes too small for you too?

482
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:42,440
Huh? What do you mean?

483
00:29:42,580 --> 00:29:44,850
Just now, you were breathing...

484
00:29:48,320 --> 00:29:50,020
like this.

485
00:29:51,150 --> 00:29:54,790
That's a trick I use when I'm feeling upset.

486
00:29:54,860 --> 00:29:56,160
If you take a deep breath...

487
00:29:57,190 --> 00:29:58,790
like this,

488
00:29:59,990 --> 00:30:01,400
and then let it all out,

489
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:04,100
it helps you feel a little better.

490
00:30:05,170 --> 00:30:07,240
But what did you mean about my clothes being too small?

491
00:30:07,470 --> 00:30:09,840
When I used to live with my mom,

492
00:30:09,900 --> 00:30:12,510
she used to do that too, just like you.

493
00:30:12,670 --> 00:30:14,040
Back then, my mom said...

494
00:30:14,110 --> 00:30:16,950
it was because she was wearing clothes that didn't fit her.

495
00:30:17,380 --> 00:30:20,420
She said it was hard to breathe.

496
00:30:23,180 --> 00:30:27,890
You're right. I guess my clothes are too small for me too.

497
00:30:40,540 --> 00:30:45,010
- You’re really out to get me today. - Well, you should visit more often,

498
00:30:45,310 --> 00:30:46,610
if it weren't for my birthday,

499
00:30:46,670 --> 00:30:50,650
- wouldn't have thought of coming? - I've been busy, that's why.

500
00:30:50,710 --> 00:30:52,780
Oh, please. That's always your excuse.

501
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:54,550
You think I have time to spare?

502
00:30:55,380 --> 00:30:56,680
But I'm here now, aren't I?

503
00:30:56,750 --> 00:30:59,690
And we brought all this to make you a birthday dinner.

504
00:30:59,750 --> 00:31:02,890
Please, I practically had to beg you, you brat. Right?

505
00:31:03,020 --> 00:31:04,360
Other people's sons...

506
00:31:04,430 --> 00:31:06,590
get married and are well supported by their in-laws.

507
00:31:08,230 --> 00:31:09,400
Oh, not this again.

508
00:31:09,460 --> 00:31:11,070
What are you trying to say?

509
00:31:11,130 --> 00:31:12,230
It's just...

510
00:31:12,300 --> 00:31:13,840
I feel sorry for you.

511
00:31:14,340 --> 00:31:16,100
You never even met your in-laws.

512
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:19,540
I mean, how could they die so tragically like that?

513
00:31:21,340 --> 00:31:22,680
Mom, be honest.

514
00:31:22,940 --> 00:31:24,250
This birthday dinner is just an excuse, isn't it?

515
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:26,280
What?

516
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:28,780
You're just doing this to give Mi Young a hard time.

517
00:31:28,850 --> 00:31:30,650
Because you don't like her.

518
00:31:31,790 --> 00:31:33,860
But why do you dislike her so much?

519
00:31:33,920 --> 00:31:35,520
What has she ever done that was so wrong?

520
00:31:35,590 --> 00:31:38,390
What are you talking about? Don't be ridiculous.

521
00:31:38,460 --> 00:31:40,500
She's your daughter-in-law, not a stranger.

522
00:31:40,560 --> 00:31:42,300
Can't you just try to like her a little?

523
00:31:42,360 --> 00:31:43,360
Quiet.

524
00:31:44,830 --> 00:31:47,540
By the way, why haven't you two had a baby?

525
00:31:48,100 --> 00:31:49,270
Where did that come from?

526
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:51,040
Tell me the truth.

527
00:31:51,170 --> 00:31:53,470
Is it Mi Young who doesn't want to have one?

528
00:31:53,540 --> 00:31:56,780
- That's it, isn't it? - That's not it.

529
00:31:56,980 --> 00:31:59,810
And if you keep this up, we'll never have a baby.

530
00:32:00,050 --> 00:32:01,050
What?

531
00:32:01,120 --> 00:32:04,050
I'm not doing this. You do it, Mom. This is so frustrating. Darn it.

532
00:32:04,820 --> 00:32:06,520
- Hey. - I knew this would happen.

533
00:32:06,590 --> 00:32:09,990
Hey, say that again.

534
00:32:10,330 --> 00:32:12,290
What did I possibly do to keep you two from having a baby?

535
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:15,360
It's true. You're always stressing us out over things like this,

536
00:32:15,430 --> 00:32:16,900
so when would we ever have time to have a baby?

537
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:18,530
Have you quite finished, you little brat?

538
00:32:18,700 --> 00:32:20,840
How have I been stressing you out?

539
00:32:23,040 --> 00:32:25,270
What's going on now? What's this all about?

540
00:32:25,410 --> 00:32:26,810
Mi Young, did you say that to Won Ho,

541
00:32:27,210 --> 00:32:29,380
that you're not getting pregnant because I'm stressing you out?

542
00:32:29,380 --> 00:32:30,380
Excuse me?

543
00:32:30,380 --> 00:32:31,450
If you hadn't said anything,

544
00:32:31,450 --> 00:32:32,580
why would he say something like that?

545
00:32:32,650 --> 00:32:33,650
Stop it.

546
00:32:36,250 --> 00:32:37,790
Because you always act like this,

547
00:32:37,850 --> 00:32:40,390
this is why I hate coming to this house. Got it?

548
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:41,660
What did you say, you brat?

549
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:44,660
- Won Ho, stop it. - Hey, Won Ho.

550
00:32:44,730 --> 00:32:45,760
You shouldn't say that.

551
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:49,230
What do you mean? Every time I come, she's dying to pick a fight.

552
00:32:49,330 --> 00:32:52,130
Get out. Get out of my house right now, you brat.

553
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:55,070
- Fine, I was leaving anyway. - Hey.

554
00:32:55,140 --> 00:32:58,140
- Goodbye. - Hey, Won Ho.

555
00:32:58,270 --> 00:32:59,270
Hey, Won Ho.

556
00:33:00,940 --> 00:33:01,940
Hey, Won Ho...

557
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:03,480
Mom...

558
00:33:03,810 --> 00:33:06,810
Just you dare come back to my house. You little brat.

559
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:08,920
- Mom, come on. - That little brat.

560
00:33:11,290 --> 00:33:12,590
That little brat.

561
00:33:19,060 --> 00:33:20,460
Did you really have to do that?

562
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:22,900
Do what?

563
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:24,430
To your mother.

564
00:33:25,100 --> 00:33:27,070
It's her birthday, after all.

565
00:33:27,870 --> 00:33:29,300
So, what? Should I have said we're having a baby?

566
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:31,270
That we'll give her a grandchild right away?

567
00:33:33,310 --> 00:33:35,380
That's why when my mom starts saying strange things,

568
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:36,540
don't just stand there and take it.

569
00:33:36,610 --> 00:33:38,610
You need to be firm about your feelings.

570
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:40,380
Because you're always so focused on your image,

571
00:33:40,450 --> 00:33:42,720
my mom thinks she can walk all over you.

572
00:33:42,950 --> 00:33:45,050
You have no problem arguing back with me.

573
00:33:45,850 --> 00:33:47,320
If this was going to happen, why did you even go?

574
00:33:47,460 --> 00:33:49,720
I told you not to go there. We went here for no reason,

575
00:33:49,790 --> 00:33:51,430
and got nothing out of it. So what was the point?

576
00:33:53,130 --> 00:33:54,130
Hey.

577
00:33:55,360 --> 00:33:58,530
What is wrong with you? Hey.

578
00:33:59,570 --> 00:34:02,670
Stop! Darn it. Hey. Hey, Baek Mi Young.

579
00:34:05,610 --> 00:34:06,710
Hey, Baek Mi Young.

580
00:34:07,180 --> 00:34:09,880
What is wrong with you? Hey!

581
00:34:30,700 --> 00:34:32,570
- Pull over. - What?

582
00:34:33,270 --> 00:34:35,770
- I said, pull over. - Why?

583
00:34:46,610 --> 00:34:48,680
What are you trying to do?

584
00:34:55,460 --> 00:34:56,460
Come on.

585
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,970
Gosh...

586
00:35:07,970 --> 00:35:08,970
Looks like your wife went all out...

587
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:10,040
on the birthday feast before she left.

588
00:35:10,470 --> 00:35:12,140
Hey, who is going to eat all this?

589
00:35:12,670 --> 00:35:14,880
Anyway, tell your wife I said thanks.

590
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:39,430
That's why when my mom starts saying strange things,

591
00:35:39,500 --> 00:35:40,570
don't just stand there and take it.

592
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:42,640
You need to be firm about your feelings.

593
00:35:42,970 --> 00:35:45,010
You have no problem arguing back with me.

594
00:35:45,170 --> 00:35:46,970
Just because you're the same age as Won Ho,

595
00:35:47,040 --> 00:35:49,140
you can't think you're the same as him. Okay?

596
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:52,250
A man can have children until the day he dies.

597
00:35:52,310 --> 00:35:54,180
Mi Young, did you say that to Won Ho,

598
00:35:54,420 --> 00:35:56,550
that you're not getting pregnant because I'm stressing you out?

599
00:35:56,850 --> 00:35:58,920
- Excuse me? - If you hadn't said anything,

600
00:35:58,990 --> 00:36:00,020
why would he say something like that?

601
00:36:36,020 --> 00:36:37,330
Please look a little to your left.

602
00:36:37,890 --> 00:36:38,890
Okay.

603
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:45,670
- Those details really pop outdoors. - Looks good.

604
00:36:47,030 --> 00:36:48,040
Wait a minute.

605
00:36:50,340 --> 00:36:52,370
Those details and the colour really stand out.

606
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:59,310
- Looks good. - Great.

607
00:36:59,380 --> 00:37:01,220
This is great.

608
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:02,480
Yes.

609
00:37:08,090 --> 00:37:09,460
(Mi Young)

610
00:37:09,520 --> 00:37:10,860
Come straight home when you're done.

611
00:37:11,490 --> 00:37:12,560
We need to talk.

612
00:37:19,470 --> 00:37:21,140
The scenery is great,

613
00:37:21,300 --> 00:37:23,200
the photos are great, and the concept is great.

614
00:37:27,410 --> 00:37:28,940
I haven't told him yet.

615
00:37:29,210 --> 00:37:31,810
What are you going to do if you still haven't told him?

616
00:37:32,150 --> 00:37:35,120
I kept meaning to tell him, but I never got the chance.

617
00:37:35,550 --> 00:37:37,590
How are you going to deal with the fallout from this?

618
00:37:39,220 --> 00:37:41,290
Actually, when he gets home today,

619
00:37:41,620 --> 00:37:43,990
I'm going to talk to him and convince him to do the reality show.

620
00:37:44,590 --> 00:37:47,060
It won't be easy, but good luck.

621
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:49,660
Okay. I'll call you back later.

622
00:37:50,160 --> 00:37:51,170
Okay.

623
00:37:57,770 --> 00:38:00,470
- Hello. - Am I speaking with Baek Mi Young?

624
00:38:01,380 --> 00:38:02,580
Yes, this is she.

625
00:38:03,180 --> 00:38:04,610
This is Maesan Hospital.

626
00:38:05,480 --> 00:38:07,520
Your husband is unconscious right now...

627
00:38:11,490 --> 00:38:14,090
These phone scammers are getting really creative.

628
00:38:23,900 --> 00:38:27,030
(Mother-In-Law's Son)

629
00:38:29,670 --> 00:38:30,970
The person you have called is unavailable...

630
00:38:30,970 --> 00:38:32,610
and will be connected to voicemail.

631
00:38:33,070 --> 00:38:34,580
Please leave your message after the tone...

632
00:38:35,080 --> 00:38:37,510
(Vice President Kang)

633
00:38:42,150 --> 00:38:45,190
Yes, Kyung Tae. Are you with Won Ho right now?

634
00:38:45,590 --> 00:38:48,090
No, he went home a while ago.

635
00:38:48,920 --> 00:38:50,020
He left a long time ago.

636
00:38:50,760 --> 00:38:51,760
Okay.

637
00:39:30,830 --> 00:39:32,270
(Mother-In-Law's Son)

638
00:39:32,330 --> 00:39:33,330
(Calling Mother-In-Law's Son)

639
00:39:36,540 --> 00:39:38,870
The person you have called is unavailable...

640
00:39:39,140 --> 00:39:40,540
(Vice President Kang)

641
00:39:40,610 --> 00:39:42,180
(Calling Vice President Kang)

642
00:39:42,580 --> 00:39:46,080
Kyung Tae, can you find out where Won Ho is right now?

643
00:39:47,110 --> 00:39:49,550
If you get in touch with Won Ho, please give me a call.

644
00:39:50,450 --> 00:39:51,450
(Vice President Kang)

645
00:39:54,460 --> 00:39:55,820
This is Maesan Hospital.

646
00:39:56,960 --> 00:39:59,030
Your husband is unconscious right now...

647
00:40:19,850 --> 00:40:21,850
(Maesan Hospital Emergency Medical Center)

648
00:40:46,470 --> 00:40:47,470
Please move out of the way.

649
00:42:06,850 --> 00:42:09,520
Daddy's right here, so don't worry.

650
00:42:10,420 --> 00:42:13,030
Daddy will protect our princesses.

651
00:42:13,090 --> 00:42:14,560
Kiss.

652
00:42:44,360 --> 00:42:45,790
He says he’s at the fishing spot right now.

653
00:42:46,430 --> 00:42:48,530
I just spoke with him, so don't worry.

654
00:43:19,490 --> 00:43:21,660
(3 Years Ago)

655
00:43:38,310 --> 00:43:40,510
- Honey. - What?

656
00:43:41,620 --> 00:43:42,620
Why?

657
00:43:43,880 --> 00:43:45,890
What is it? Were you having a nightmare?

658
00:43:50,290 --> 00:43:54,060
Yes, something terrifying was chasing me.

659
00:43:55,460 --> 00:43:58,930
I tried to run away, but my feet were stuck.

660
00:44:00,170 --> 00:44:01,370
It was so scary.

661
00:44:01,570 --> 00:44:04,670
You should have called for me.

662
00:44:05,540 --> 00:44:06,810
You're all sweaty.

663
00:44:13,350 --> 00:44:14,350
Ta-da.

664
00:44:15,650 --> 00:44:18,390
Were you scared, Princess Dallae?

665
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:22,060
Daddy's right here, so don't worry.

666
00:44:23,520 --> 00:44:26,130
Daddy will protect our princesses.

667
00:44:26,190 --> 00:44:27,800
Kiss.

668
00:44:33,630 --> 00:44:34,940
Are you leaving for work already?

669
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:38,010
Yes, I have a lot to do today. I have to go out for work.

670
00:44:38,440 --> 00:44:41,240
- You get more rest and come later. - You're going out for work?

671
00:44:42,080 --> 00:44:44,240
Yes, with Ms. Kwon.

672
00:44:44,610 --> 00:44:45,610
What?

673
00:44:48,180 --> 00:44:50,520
So I have to close up by myself again today?

674
00:44:51,620 --> 00:44:54,020
I'm sorry. Today's the last day. It will all be over today.

675
00:44:54,620 --> 00:44:58,660
How many times have you said that? I seriously want to cry.

676
00:44:59,160 --> 00:45:01,160
I know. I thought it would be over sooner too,

677
00:45:01,300 --> 00:45:02,560
but it's taking longer than expected.

678
00:45:03,700 --> 00:45:04,800
But honey,

679
00:45:06,030 --> 00:45:09,640
can't you please not go today?

680
00:45:10,140 --> 00:45:13,070
I'm feeling anxious because of the dream I had.

681
00:45:13,140 --> 00:45:16,980
- I don't feel well either. - Today is the last day.

682
00:45:19,510 --> 00:45:22,120
So to you,

683
00:45:22,580 --> 00:45:24,420
Ms. Kwon is more important than me and Dallae.

684
00:45:25,390 --> 00:45:26,550
How can you say that?

685
00:45:26,620 --> 00:45:28,820
Who do you think I'm working this hard for?

686
00:45:31,060 --> 00:45:32,760
I'm making wedding attire for multicultural couples...

687
00:45:32,830 --> 00:45:34,390
who are struggling financially.

688
00:45:34,560 --> 00:45:37,160
And Ms. Kwon said she would do a lot of promotion for us.

689
00:45:37,430 --> 00:45:40,770
But it's just too hard for me to do it alone without you.

690
00:45:42,270 --> 00:45:44,710
Then just leave anything that's too difficult.

691
00:45:44,940 --> 00:45:46,770
I'll come back as soon as I can and finish up.

692
00:45:49,580 --> 00:45:51,110
Honey, please,

693
00:45:51,380 --> 00:45:54,820
don't go today. Please?

694
00:46:08,300 --> 00:46:09,400
Yes, hello?

695
00:46:10,060 --> 00:46:13,730
Yes, I'm sorry. It's not ready yet.

696
00:46:14,900 --> 00:46:17,670
Five meters of lace.

697
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:20,670
- Lace. - And...

698
00:46:21,980 --> 00:46:23,880
ten bolts of silk.

699
00:46:28,320 --> 00:46:30,520
Don't overdo it. Just leave anything that's too difficult,

700
00:46:30,580 --> 00:46:32,050
and I'll do it as soon as I get back.

701
00:46:32,690 --> 00:46:33,790
I'll be right back, okay?

702
00:46:33,890 --> 00:46:34,890
I'll be back soon.

703
00:46:57,840 --> 00:47:00,050
Hello, Ms. Kwon. I'm on my way now.

704
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:51,630
(Operating Room)

705
00:48:33,270 --> 00:48:35,480
I'm so sorry, but the baby...

706
00:48:56,460 --> 00:48:57,800
You should just rest.

707
00:49:04,070 --> 00:49:05,070
Don't throw it away.

708
00:49:05,370 --> 00:49:07,540
- Just leave it. - No.

709
00:49:10,510 --> 00:49:13,080
Looking at it will just be a painful reminder.

710
00:49:47,180 --> 00:49:48,450
Don't get sentimental.

711
00:49:49,580 --> 00:49:51,280
You don't have the right.

712
00:49:55,060 --> 00:49:56,620
Now that Dallae's gone,

713
00:49:57,720 --> 00:49:59,330
there's nothing holding you back anymore.

714
00:50:01,090 --> 00:50:03,430
You can do whatever you like now.

715
00:50:04,630 --> 00:50:05,630
What?

716
00:50:06,470 --> 00:50:08,740
You can even do all the volunteering you want.

717
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,070
How can you say that right now?

718
00:50:13,840 --> 00:50:15,310
When we lost Dallae,

719
00:50:16,910 --> 00:50:18,510
you weren't there for us.

720
00:50:20,110 --> 00:50:21,110
I...

721
00:50:23,350 --> 00:50:25,120
I was all alone again.

722
00:50:31,890 --> 00:50:32,890
That day...

723
00:50:33,990 --> 00:50:35,360
From that morning,

724
00:50:37,030 --> 00:50:41,640
something felt so wrong. I felt so anxious.

725
00:50:42,140 --> 00:50:43,740
I told you not to go.

726
00:50:45,310 --> 00:50:47,140
I begged you not to leave.

727
00:50:49,540 --> 00:50:50,540
Dallae.

728
00:50:51,610 --> 00:50:53,050
It's your fault this happened.

729
00:50:53,310 --> 00:50:55,520
How was I supposed to know every detail about your condition?

730
00:50:55,580 --> 00:50:56,820
The baby was inside you.

731
00:50:57,520 --> 00:50:58,520
What?

732
00:50:59,720 --> 00:51:01,290
Inside me?

733
00:51:03,160 --> 00:51:04,160
No.

734
00:51:05,260 --> 00:51:06,260
I...

735
00:51:06,830 --> 00:51:08,060
I still...

736
00:51:08,860 --> 00:51:11,670
I still feel like Dallae is right here.

737
00:51:12,670 --> 00:51:15,670
I feel like she's still here playing.

738
00:51:19,610 --> 00:51:20,840
It feels like if I just wait a little longer,

739
00:51:20,910 --> 00:51:22,940
I'll be able to see her.

740
00:51:28,050 --> 00:51:29,050
Mi Young.

741
00:51:29,450 --> 00:51:32,720
- Give that to me. I'll... - No. This...

742
00:51:32,990 --> 00:51:35,490
This is our Dallae's toy.

743
00:51:36,190 --> 00:51:38,460
It's her toy. I can't let her go.

744
00:51:39,690 --> 00:51:43,260
Mommy is so sorry. I'm so sorry I couldn't protect you.

745
00:51:43,830 --> 00:51:44,830
Mommy...

746
00:51:46,200 --> 00:51:47,300
Dallae...

747
00:51:48,770 --> 00:51:49,840
I'm so sorry.

748
00:52:33,580 --> 00:52:34,810
What are you doing sitting in the dark?

749
00:52:42,820 --> 00:52:45,790
Well, the weather was so nice for a change.

750
00:52:47,560 --> 00:52:49,560
And I happened to be near a freshwater fishing spot.

751
00:52:49,630 --> 00:52:51,600
I even caught a fish. A really big one. Want to see it?

752
00:52:52,370 --> 00:52:53,730
Why didn't you answer your phone?

753
00:52:57,640 --> 00:53:00,570
You told me to come straight home. If I answered, you'd nag...

754
00:53:04,280 --> 00:53:06,080
I knew you'd just yell at me.

755
00:53:07,350 --> 00:53:09,580
So 26 missed calls...

756
00:53:10,620 --> 00:53:12,390
just looked like me nagging you?

757
00:53:15,060 --> 00:53:16,060
I'm sorry.

758
00:53:32,170 --> 00:53:34,340
(Dream Project: Wedding Edition)

759
00:53:41,380 --> 00:53:42,820
I don't think I can hear it.

760
00:53:43,080 --> 00:53:45,750
Isn't CEO Baek incredible?

761
00:53:46,720 --> 00:53:47,720
She got CEO Ji...

762
00:53:47,790 --> 00:53:48,790
who swore he'd never do a variety show.

763
00:53:49,120 --> 00:53:53,630
- How did she convince him? - Oh, don't even get me started.

764
00:53:54,030 --> 00:53:56,160
My stomach was in knots just watching.

765
00:53:57,260 --> 00:53:59,500
What? Your stomach was in knots?

766
00:54:00,130 --> 00:54:03,170
It's an expression.

767
00:54:04,800 --> 00:54:05,810
Hello.

768
00:54:05,810 --> 00:54:07,270
Oh, I'm so sorry. The weather's so cold,

769
00:54:07,340 --> 00:54:08,780
and we ended up having to shoot outdoors.

770
00:54:08,840 --> 00:54:11,980
We can handle a little cold. Right, CEO Ji?

771
00:54:13,310 --> 00:54:14,880
Oh, yes. I'm fine as well.

772
00:54:16,250 --> 00:54:18,590
We would've preferred to shoot indoors,

773
00:54:18,820 --> 00:54:21,660
but the participant's dream is to have a wedding on a boat.

774
00:54:22,120 --> 00:54:23,660
In any case, we look forward to working with you.

775
00:54:23,990 --> 00:54:24,990
Of course.

776
00:54:26,760 --> 00:54:29,730
You put all this together in just one day?

777
00:54:29,800 --> 00:54:32,030
It looks like it would've taken a long time.

778
00:54:32,770 --> 00:54:33,770
Excuse me?

779
00:54:33,830 --> 00:54:35,270
Oh, we couldn't do it in just one day.

780
00:54:35,640 --> 00:54:37,300
It took us several days just to secure the boat.

781
00:54:37,970 --> 00:54:38,970
What?

782
00:54:39,540 --> 00:54:41,710
This is all thanks to the two of you.

783
00:54:42,140 --> 00:54:44,210
Because you agreed to our offer on the day I approached you,

784
00:54:44,280 --> 00:54:46,050
we were able to line up our filming schedule perfectly.

785
00:54:47,010 --> 00:54:48,010
What did you say?

786
00:54:49,120 --> 00:54:51,120
Yes, are we heading to the shoot now?

787
00:54:51,180 --> 00:54:52,850
Wait a minute. What is this all about?

788
00:54:53,250 --> 00:54:56,220
We agreed on the day we were asked? I only said I would do it yesterday.

789
00:54:56,860 --> 00:54:57,890
Oh, about that...

790
00:55:00,360 --> 00:55:01,360
I'm sorry.

791
00:55:01,530 --> 00:55:05,230
I told her beforehand that we'd do it.

792
00:55:05,670 --> 00:55:07,370
I was going to tell you later.

793
00:55:09,700 --> 00:55:12,240
So, shall we get going?

794
00:55:12,310 --> 00:55:14,210
- Yes. - No.

795
00:55:14,870 --> 00:55:15,980
I'm not doing the shoot.

796
00:55:19,610 --> 00:55:21,750
CEO Baek, you're really going too far now.

797
00:55:22,280 --> 00:55:24,350
So have you been lying to me this whole time?

798
00:55:25,890 --> 00:55:27,050
What's wrong with you? People are watching.

799
00:55:27,120 --> 00:55:28,120
Keep your voice down.

800
00:55:28,190 --> 00:55:29,920
And what if I don't?

801
00:55:30,120 --> 00:55:31,360
Everyone here deserves to know...

802
00:55:31,420 --> 00:55:33,460
how you tricked me and do what you want.

803
00:55:42,440 --> 00:55:43,440
It's just...

804
00:55:44,870 --> 00:55:48,040
I didn't mean to trick you from the beginning.

805
00:55:48,370 --> 00:55:50,480
I just missed the right time to tell you.

806
00:55:50,610 --> 00:55:52,710
Oh, you missed the right time? Why?

807
00:55:52,850 --> 00:55:54,480
You might as well say you sent it telepathically.

808
00:55:54,550 --> 00:55:56,220
It's true, really.

809
00:55:56,380 --> 00:55:58,550
No, Won Ho, you never gave me a chance to talk.

810
00:55:58,620 --> 00:56:00,390
Oh, cut the act. Seriously.

811
00:56:01,250 --> 00:56:02,760
Your mom's birthday dinner,

812
00:56:02,820 --> 00:56:04,490
the 26 calls you made yesterday,

813
00:56:04,560 --> 00:56:05,990
it was all an act, wasn't it?

814
00:56:06,060 --> 00:56:07,530
You knew that I'd get weak...

815
00:56:07,590 --> 00:56:09,330
and give you permission. You calculated it all.

816
00:56:09,400 --> 00:56:10,730
You already had the answer you wanted...

817
00:56:10,800 --> 00:56:12,530
and made a fool out of me, didn't you?

818
00:56:12,600 --> 00:56:15,100
That wasn't entirely about the show.

819
00:56:15,170 --> 00:56:18,770
- This is really annoying. - No, Won Ho.

820
00:56:18,840 --> 00:56:19,940
Hey, Won Ho.

821
00:56:23,840 --> 00:56:24,840
Won Ho.

822
00:56:24,980 --> 00:56:26,380
Won Ho, can we talk for a minute?

823
00:56:26,910 --> 00:56:27,910
Won Ho.

824
00:56:28,850 --> 00:56:30,680
- Wait. - Move.

825
00:56:30,820 --> 00:56:31,820
Wait, hold on.

826
00:56:33,750 --> 00:56:34,750
Right now,

827
00:56:34,820 --> 00:56:36,360
our employees and the production crew...

828
00:56:36,360 --> 00:56:39,590
are all waiting for you. If you say you're not doing it now,

829
00:56:39,660 --> 00:56:41,190
what about all the production costs?

830
00:56:41,260 --> 00:56:44,560
Then what about me? I'm so furious that you tricked me...

831
00:56:44,630 --> 00:56:46,530
that I can't do this show or anything else.

832
00:56:46,600 --> 00:56:48,230
What about me? What am I supposed to do?

833
00:56:48,300 --> 00:56:50,340
But I didn't have a choice.

834
00:56:50,770 --> 00:56:52,570
If I hadn't accepted the offer that day,

835
00:56:52,740 --> 00:56:54,770
the appearance would have been cancelled.

836
00:56:54,940 --> 00:56:56,580
What? Would the world end if the appearance was cancelled?

837
00:56:56,640 --> 00:56:57,640
Would we starve to death?

838
00:56:58,180 --> 00:57:00,510
Fine, it was all my fault.

839
00:57:00,580 --> 00:57:01,710
I'm so sorry.

840
00:57:01,780 --> 00:57:03,720
I tricked you and made a fool out of you.

841
00:57:03,780 --> 00:57:07,050
That's all my fault. So please, just this once, okay?

842
00:57:07,390 --> 00:57:08,390
No.

843
00:57:09,320 --> 00:57:11,190
Not for me, for our shop.

844
00:57:11,260 --> 00:57:13,660
Stop using the shop as an excuse. This is all about your greed.

845
00:57:13,790 --> 00:57:16,200
This all happened because you were greedy.

846
00:57:18,360 --> 00:57:19,370
So...

847
00:57:20,770 --> 00:57:22,200
you refuse to do it, no matter what?

848
00:57:22,540 --> 00:57:23,770
Yes. Move.

849
00:57:29,780 --> 00:57:30,780
Wait.

850
00:57:32,080 --> 00:57:33,610
I'm not done talking.

851
00:57:35,320 --> 00:57:36,320
What now?

852
00:57:38,520 --> 00:57:41,020
Fine. I'm...

853
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:44,960
What was that?

854
00:57:46,630 --> 00:57:47,760
I've made up my mind.

855
00:57:53,100 --> 00:57:54,100
Let's get...

856
00:57:54,930 --> 00:57:56,900
What are you saying? Speak up, I can't hear you.

857
00:58:23,100 --> 00:58:26,000
(Epilogue)

858
00:58:34,070 --> 00:58:36,710
We scraped together every penny we had...

859
00:58:36,780 --> 00:58:38,080
for our new apartment.

860
00:58:38,950 --> 00:58:40,280
And the ceiling is leaking?

861
00:58:40,780 --> 00:58:41,780
Are you serious?

862
00:58:41,980 --> 00:58:43,420
Come on. Still, for people like us,

863
00:58:43,480 --> 00:58:45,720
getting a place this big near the city is a stroke of luck.

864
00:58:46,590 --> 00:58:47,750
Let's look on the bright side.

865
00:58:48,760 --> 00:58:50,760
We can just call someone to fix the ceiling tomorrow.

866
00:58:50,990 --> 00:58:52,860
Still, it's upsetting just looking at it.

867
00:58:53,790 --> 00:58:54,790
It's unsettling.

868
00:58:57,560 --> 00:58:58,730
Then how about we do this?

869
00:59:05,710 --> 00:59:09,540
- How's that? - For a leak, that's not much water.

870
00:59:09,840 --> 00:59:10,840
You think so?

871
00:59:11,210 --> 00:59:12,710
Then should I just bust a hole in the ceiling?

872
00:59:12,780 --> 00:59:14,350
So water comes pouring out like a waterfall?

873
00:59:14,980 --> 00:59:16,150
The house would collapse.

874
00:59:20,290 --> 00:59:21,720
I know things are tough right now,

875
00:59:21,720 --> 00:59:23,160
but please be patient a little longer.

876
00:59:23,890 --> 00:59:25,190
I promise I'll make it big, no matter what.

877
00:59:25,260 --> 00:59:27,530
I'll make sure you get to live in a house like a palace.

878
00:59:28,390 --> 00:59:30,100
So confident.

879
00:59:31,330 --> 00:59:33,170
All right. I believe you.

880
00:59:36,840 --> 00:59:37,900
And what's that...

881
00:59:38,440 --> 00:59:41,040
What's with that other look of confidence?

882
00:59:42,540 --> 00:59:43,640
Since we're bored,

883
00:59:44,480 --> 00:59:45,810
why don't we go to our room for a bit?

884
00:59:46,010 --> 00:59:48,450
Go to our room because we're bored?

885
00:59:48,510 --> 00:59:51,020
What? Let's just go lie down in our room for a bit.

886
00:59:51,080 --> 00:59:53,620
Let's just hang out here. Why do we have to go to our room?

887
00:59:53,690 --> 00:59:55,220
Why? Come on, you're tired.

888
00:59:55,290 --> 00:59:58,760
- What's gotten into you? Suddenly? - No, my knee.

889
00:59:59,230 --> 01:00:00,830
- What's wrong? - Seriously, my knee...

890
01:00:00,890 --> 01:00:01,890
Come here.

891
01:00:02,160 --> 01:00:04,430
Hey, I got you.

892
01:00:18,850 --> 01:00:21,780
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

893
01:00:22,280 --> 01:00:24,920
- Why do you think I threw it? - That was a real Cartier.

894
01:00:24,980 --> 01:00:25,990
So what?

895
01:00:26,050 --> 01:00:27,320
It was a limited edition.

896
01:00:27,390 --> 01:00:28,390
Hey.

897
01:00:29,660 --> 01:00:31,360
I just couldn't believe it.

898
01:00:31,490 --> 01:00:34,290
- Is that really Cheon Man Ju? - She's a Gen Z and millennial icon.

899
01:00:34,360 --> 01:00:36,260
I'm a huge fan of yours.

900
01:00:36,530 --> 01:00:37,700
You throw parties too?

901
01:00:37,760 --> 01:00:38,770
Are you crazy?

902
01:00:38,830 --> 01:00:40,100
You're thinking of going to the Calvin Hotel?

903
01:00:40,170 --> 01:00:42,640
Whatever harm Calvin might do to me now...

904
01:00:42,840 --> 01:00:44,140
is just a drop in the bucket...

905
01:00:44,200 --> 01:00:45,940
compared to how you've torn me apart.

906
01:00:46,010 --> 01:00:47,810
Even if Calvin is divorced,

907
01:00:47,870 --> 01:00:49,540
he wouldn't actually hit on Mi Young, would he?

908
01:00:50,240 --> 01:00:51,640
Why do I have such a bad feeling about this?

909
01:00:51,710 --> 01:00:52,780
Something just feels off.

910
01:00:53,180 --> 01:00:54,180
It's been a while.
